# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only

# Build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT (the Dockerfile COPYs engine/..., the
# workspace pyproject.toml and uv.lock, and LICENSE -- which lives at the root
# for AGPL compliance, see Dockerfile step 2a). Everything the image does not
# need is excluded here so the context stays small.

# Never ship a locally built environment or a tool cache. The image restores its
# own from uv.lock, and a host virtualenv carries absolute paths that are wrong
# inside a container.
.venv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# VCS / editor noise
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Untracked working files -- never part of an image.
CLAUDE.md
.private/
.token-optimizer/
.fastembed_cache/

# Layers that are not the engine. TWO paths under backend/ are re-admitted
# below, and each earns its place: uv must be able to load every workspace
# member to honour the single root uv.lock, and import-linter must be able to
# build a graph that names econflow_backend as a root package -- without the
# source it reports a broken contract instead of a held one. No backend code
# runs in this image either way.
backend/
!backend/pyproject.toml
!backend/src/**
frontend/
deploy/
# docs/ is not listed because there is no docs/ directory. It was removed from
# the tree, no command here recreates it, and an exclusion naming a path nothing
# produces tells a reader the tree holds something it does not.
# .github/ is excluded, with THREE exceptions re-admitted below: the manifest
# that run_verifications.sh reads its anti-vacuity floor from, and the two gate
# scripts steps 9 and 10 of that suite shell out to by path. Without the manifest
# the floor silently degrades and the image's hard build gate stops asserting a
# minimum. Without the scripts, bash exits 127 on a file that is not there, the
# suite's `|| fail` fires, and the build dies printing "FAIL: a wrapper reaches
# the network" -- measured on 2026-08-22, accusing the wrapper tree of a network
# call when the real cause is an uncopied file. Both halves are required: a COPY
# alone cannot reach a path this file excludes.
.github/
!.github/inventory.json
!.github/scripts/check-no-network.sh
!.github/actions/assert-inventory/assert.sh

# docs that never enter the container
*.md.bak
